{"id": "section-body-00570", "title": "Cardiac Arrest and Cardiopulmonary Resuscitation", "chapterId": "chapter-one", "blocks": [{"id": "body-00570", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading2", "text": "Cardiac Arrest and Cardiopulmonary Resuscitation", "runs": [{"text": "Cardiac"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Arrest"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "and"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Cardiopulmonary"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Resuscitation"}], "level": 2, "list": {"level": 1, "numberingId": "1890"}}, {"id": "body-00571", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Cardiopulmonary resuscitation is an emergency lifesaving procedure performed when there is a sudden cessation of heartbeat. It involves the combination of chest compression and artificial ventilation to preserve blood flow to the organs including the brain function. Early initiation of CPR can double or triple the chances of survival after cardiac arrest.", "runs": [{"text": "Cardiopulmonary resuscitation is an emergency lifesaving procedure performed when there is a sudden cessation of heartbeat. It involves the combination of chest compression and artificial ventilation to preserve blood flow to the organs including the brain function. Early initiation of CPR can double or triple the chances of survival after cardiac arrest."}]}, {"id": "body-00572-textbox1-00001", "type": "paragraph", "style": "Normal", "text": "Note: HIGH QUALITY CPR", "runs": [{"text": "Note:", "bold": true}, {"text": " ", "bold": true}, {"text": "HIGH QUALITY", "bold": true}, {"text": " ", "bold": true}, {"text": "CPR", "bold": true}]}, {"id": "body-00572-textbox1-00002", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Compressions:", "runs": [{"text": "Compressions:"}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1887"}}, {"id": "body-00572-textbox1-00003", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Infant: heel of one hand (if alone) or thumb encircling technique (if you have assistance)", "runs": [{"text": "Infant:"}, {"text": " "}, 